Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 22:28:12 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 28/28] kk: Avoid kernel panic due to out of device memory in Metal

Metal doesn't handle correctly out of device memory resulting in a kernel
panic. Limit allocations to 95% of suggested maximum memory usage by Metal.

Upstream Mesa 0db4e290a0a2d95709203abd45f21f464b71f24c, hand-ported onto this
series (kk_alloc_bo takes a memory category here; the workaround mask is
resolved in kk_resolve_workarounds). KK_WORKAROUND_20, disabled on macOS 27
(MESA_KK_DISABLE_WORKAROUNDS=20 turns it off). No codegen change.

Upstream-author: Aitor Camacho
Reviewed-by: squidbus
Signed-off-by: Aitor Camacho
Part-of: <https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/46368>
Generated-by: LLM
